{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat assignments/T-N-build-cmake-flags.md'","aggregated_output":"# Assignment T-N (campaign c2-resume, host x86-main, owner: Claude Opus; worker: Codex)\nQuestion: let the Build CC produce engine variants that need extra CMake options (first consumer: -DGGML_CUDA_NO_VMM=ON so the gpu_budget LD_PRELOAD shim sees allocations; see cc/gpu_budget/README.md \"Using with the engine\"), and add a post-build linkage check.\nPinned base: commit 712fcd5. Read cc/build_engine/{README.md,build_engine.py,test_build_engine.py} and the Dockerfile/bake it generates.\nAllowed writes: cc/build_engine/** and artifacts/codexN/. Nothing else.\nRequired: (a) repeatable `--cmake-define KEY=VALUE` (validate KEY matches ^[A-Z0-9_]+$, VALUE has no whitespace/shell metacharacters; reject duplicates/conflicts with built-in flags); defines are passed as a build arg, appear in the recipe hash and build-record.json (schema bump to 2, keep reading of v1 records if any code reads them) and as an image label; (b) a new optional post-build step `linkage` that, in a short-lived `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only` of the built image config ID, runs `ldd` on /app/libggml-cuda.so (find actual name) and `readelf -Ws` / or nm -D to record: whether libcudart is dynamically linked, and whether cudaMalloc/cudaFree/cudaMemGetInfo are undefined imports; result recorded in build-record.json under `linkage` with raw outputs saved to files; failure of this step is recorded, not fatal only if the user passed --linkage-optional (default: fatal? choose: record failure_stage='linkage' and exit nonzero). Be explicit if a tool is missing in the runtime image (record unavailable + reason, not false).\nTests: extend test_build_engine.py with unit tests (no Docker) for define validation, recipe-hash change, record schema, linkage parser on captured ldd/readelf fixture text.\nLimits: 30 min, no network, no Docker execution (orchestrator runs the real build). Final message: diff summary, pytest command/result, exact CLI the orchestrator should run for the NO_VMM variant, gaps.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
