{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat cc/build_engine/README.md cc/build_engine/build_engine.py cc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat cc/build_engine/README.md cc/build_engine/build_engine.py cc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py'","aggregated_output":"# build_engine\n\nUse this capability to turn a clean, identified local llama.cpp checkout and an optional Git patch into a local, runtime-only CUDA image and an evidence directory. It targets linux/amd64 and CUDA architecture 120 (RTX 5070 Ti). Model weights are supplied separately at runtime.\n\nRequires Python 3.12+ (stdlib only), Git, Docker daemon access, and Docker Buildx/Bake. pytest is needed only for tests. No GPU is needed to compile or collect hashes. The builder installs Ubuntu build packages with apt; an actual build needs cached packages/base layers or repository/registry access. This implementation does not download source, patches, models, or web UI assets. The existing `campaign/cuda-tools:c1` image is not used as the builder because the required builder base is the digest-pinned NVIDIA devel image.\n\n## Run\n\nRun from the campaign directory. Give every attempt a new or empty output directory. While executing assignment T-D, keep outputs under `cc/build_engine/` or `builds/llamacpp/`.\n\n```bash\n# Supply the real runtime image digest from trusted/local image evidence.\nexport BASE_RUNTIME='nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-runtime-ubuntu24.04@sha256:<64-hex-digest>'\npython3 cc/build_engine/build_engine.py \\\n  --source ref/llama.cpp --commit 31288c9c6 \\\n  --tag campaign/llamacpp:c1 --out cc/build_engine/results/baseline\n```\n\nThe placeholder must be replaced; it is not a working digest. If BASE_RUNTIME is unset, the CLI inspects the local runtime tag and selects its NVIDIA RepoDigest without pulling it. Missing local images or RepoDigests fail at `base_images`. BASE_DEVEL defaults to the devel digest already recorded in `artifacts/op-309e1f95c716/stdout`; override it with a full `nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-devel-ubuntu24.04@sha256:...` reference when needed. Both bases are validated and supplied as separate name and digest Dockerfile arguments. The CLI never builds from a floating base tag.\n\nTo add a patch, save a unified Git diff to a file and add `--patch path/to/change.patch`. Source HEAD must resolve to `--commit`; tracked changes and untracked files cause rejection. The source checkout remains read-only: Git optional locks are disabled, a `git archive` snapshot is extracted under the output directory, and `git apply --check` runs there before `git apply`. Git discovery stops before the enclosing campaign repository. Binary patches supported by Git are accepted. Submodules are rejected. Git archive honors committed export attributes; ignored and untracked files and `.git` are omitted. Docker ignore files in the staged snapshot are emptied to prevent omission of tracked source. Temporary staging is removed after either result. Keep the supplied patch and original commit for rebuilding; patch bytes are identified by SHA256 but are not retained as a separate output artifact.\n\nThe image contains only the seven requested tools in `/app`, their generated shared libraries and the OpenMP runtime, on top of the CUDA runtime base. It has no compiler, source checkout, or weights. Its entrypoint is cleared, so invoke tools by full path, for example `/app/llama-bench`. Release/shared CUDA compilation uses the flags in `build-record.json`; CPU-native tuning, tests, downloaded UI, and OpenSSL are disabled. `LLAMA_CURL=OFF` is passed as requested, although this checkout treats LLAMA_CURL as deprecated. Source and patch identity are recorded as image labels; binaries' built-in Git version may say `unknown` because `.git` is not staged.\n\n## Outputs and failure handling\n\n`build-record.json` uses schema version 1. It records status, failure stage/error, requested and resolved commit, Git tree ID and dirty status, patch SHA256 or null, tag/platform, recipe SHA256 and sizes, base references/digests, Docker and Buildx versions, CMake flags, Buildx metadata, image config ID/RepoDigests/Created/Architecture/Os, tool SHA256 values, saved archive SHA256/bytes, build duration and total duration. Fields remain null or empty when a failure occurs before collection. `build_wall_seconds` measures the Bake invocation, including export; `wall_seconds` covers the whole attempt.\n\nThe other files are:\n\n- `build.stdout` and `build.stderr`: full subprocess stdout/stderr, including compiler output and diagnostics on failure. Binary Git archive output is directed to staging rather than the logs.\n- `buildx-metadata.json`: Buildx metadata, when the build produces it; retained even when the build exits nonzero.\n- `engine-image.docker.tar`: `docker save` of the built immutable image config ID, on success. Its bytes and SHA256 are recorded after saving.\n\nThe CLI exits 0 only after all evidence collection succeeds, otherwise nonzero. Failures include source mismatch/dirty tree, unsupported submodules, malformed or inapplicable patch, unavailable Docker/base image, build/export failure, incorrect architecture, missing binaries, save failure, or malformed archive. A failure after building can leave the tagged local image and partial evidence; inspect `failure_stage` and retry in a fresh output directory. Invalid CLI arguments, an unwritable output path, or a nonempty output directory fail before a record can be created. Existing evidence is never overwritten. The CLI does not push, prune, mount the Docker socket in an image, or operate on unrelated containers. A single short-lived `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /usr/bin/sha256sum` container hashes the tools without requesting a GPU. Subsequent hashing and saving use the immutable config ID so a later tag change cannot change the evidence target.\n\nBake requests maximum provenance and saves metadata separately. This does not imply provenance survives image loading and `docker save`. The archive inspector checks `index.json` and reachable OCI manifests for actual in-toto SLSA provenance statements. A classic Docker archive without an OCI index records `retained: false`; an SBOM or an attestation annotation alone does not count. A save or inspection failure leaves provenance unconfirmed. No signature or attestation trust verification is performed.\n\n## Validation without a build\n\nFrom `builds/llamacpp/`, run `docker buildx bake --print`; the retained `bake-print.json` is the validated default expansion. Its runtime digest is intentionally empty until supplied; print mode validates Bake syntax, not base availability or compilation. For a direct Bake build, supply digest-pinned BASE_DEVEL and BASE_RUNTIME plus SOURCE_DIR, SOURCE_COMMIT and PATCH_SHA256, and use a prepared staging snapshot. Prefer the CLI, which verifies those inputs. Bake uses `BAKE_CMD_CONTEXT` to locate the recipe Dockerfile outside the source context; invoke it from the recipe directory.\n\nFrom the campaign directory, run:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m pytest -q \\\n  cc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py \\\n  --basetemp=cc/build_engine/.pytest-tmp \\\n  -o cache_dir=cc/build_engine/.pytest_cache\n```\n\nTests use temporary Git repositories and mocked Docker subprocesses. They cover patch rejection, successful patch isolation, successful record schema, build failure logs/metadata, dirty or mismatched source, archive/tool hashing, provenance versus SBOM, and refusing to overwrite evidence. They use no network, GPU, or real build.\n\nThis evidence does not prove bitwise reproducibility, runtime correctness, model accuracy, GPU compatibility/performance, or the absence of vulnerabilities. Apt package versions, compiler behavior, timestamps, and upstream build scripts can vary. Base digests and input hashes identify inputs; they do not establish equivalence to an upstream image. The orchestrator must perform the real build and runtime checks. No full build was performed for T-D.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Build a local CUDA engine and record evidence; uses only the Python stdlib.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport shutil\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport tarfile\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nRECIPES = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / \"builds\" / \"llamacpp\"\nTOOLS = (\"llama-bench\", \"llama-perplexity\", \"llama-completion\", \"llama-server\",\n         \"llama-eval-callback\", \"llama-cli\", \"llama-tokenize\")\nCMAKE_FLAGS = [\"-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\", \"-DGGML_CUDA=ON\",\n               \"-DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=120\", \"-DLLAMA_CURL=OFF\",\n               \"-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON\", \"-DGGML_NATIVE=OFF\",\n               \"-DLLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=OFF\", \"-DLLAMA_BUILD_UI=OFF\",\n               \"-DLLAMA_USE_PREBUILT_UI=OFF\", \"-DLLAMA_OPENSSL=OFF\"]\nDEFAULT_DEVEL = (\"nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-devel-ubuntu24.04@sha256:\"\n                 \"520292dbb4f755fd360766059e62956e9379485d9e073bbd2f6e3c20c270ed66\")\nDEFAULT_RUNTIME = \"nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-runtime-ubuntu24.04\"\n\n\ndef file_digest(path):\n    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n    size = 0\n    with Path(path).open(\"rb\") as stream:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: stream.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n            digest.update(chunk)\n            size += len(chunk)\n    return {\"sha256\": digest.hexdigest(), \"bytes\": size}\n\n\ndef archive_identities(path):\n    \"\"\"Distinct identities from a `docker save` archive: config digest (image config), top-level index digest (what the containerd store\n    reports as `Id`), and image-manifest digests. Never conflate them: only the config digest is the classic image ID.\"\"\"\n    out = {\"config_digest\": None, \"index_digest\": None, \"index_manifests\": []}\n    with tarfile.open(path) as t:\n        names = t.getnames()\n        if \"manifest.json\" in names:\n            m = json.load(t.extractfile(\"manifest.json\"))\n            if m and m[0].get(\"Config\", \"\").startswith(\"blobs/sha256/\"):\n                out[\"config_digest\"] = \"sha256:\" + m[0][\"Config\"].split(\"/\")[-1]\n        if \"index.json\" in names:\n            raw = t.extractfile(\"index.json\").read()\n            idx = json.loads(raw)\n            out[\"index_manifests\"] = [{\"digest\": d.get(\"digest\"), \"mediaType\": d.get(\"mediaType\")} for d in idx.get(\"manifests\", [])]\n            out[\"index_digest\"] = out[\"index_manifests\"][0][\"digest\"] if len(out[\"index_manifests\"]) == 1 else None\n            out[\"index_entry_digests\"] = [d[\"digest\"] for d in out[\"index_manifests\"]]   # may include an attestation manifest next to the image manifest\n    return out\n\n\ndef archive_provenance(path):\n    \"\"\"Follow only manifests reachable from the saved archive's OCI index.\"\"\"\n    with tarfile.open(path, \"r:*\") as archive:\n        names = {member.name.removeprefix(\"./\"): member for member in archive}\n\n        def read_json(name):\n            member = names.get(name)\n            if member is None:\n                raise ValueError(\"missing OCI manifest: \" + name)\n            with archive.extractfile(member) as stream:\n                return json.load(stream)\n\n        if \"index.json\" not in names:\n            return {\"retained\": False, \"reason\": \"No OCI index.json in docker save archive\",\n                    \"attestation_manifests\": []}\n        found, seen = [], set()\n\n        def visit(desc, attestation=False):\n            digest = desc.get(\"digest\", \"\")\n            if not re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", digest) or digest in seen:\n                return\n            seen.add(digest)\n            name = \"blobs/sha256/\" + digest.split(\":\")[1]\n            doc = read_json(name)\n            marked = (attestation or desc.get(\"annotations\", {}).get(\n                \"vnd.docker.reference.type\") == \"attestation-manifest\")\n            for layer in doc.get(\"layers\", []):\n                if layer.get(\"mediaType\") != \"application/vnd.in-toto+json\":\n                    continue\n                statement = read_json(\"blobs/sha256/\" + layer[\"digest\"].split(\":\")[1])\n                if statement.get(\"predicateType\", \"\").startswith(\"https://slsa.dev/provenance/\"):\n                    # The in-toto predicate itself proves this is provenance, not just an SBOM.\n                    found.append({\"manifest\": digest, \"statement\": layer[\"digest\"],\n                                  \"predicate_type\": statement[\"predicateType\"],\n                                  \"attestation_annotation\": marked})\n            for child in doc.get(\"manifests\", []):\n                visit(child, marked)\n\n        for descriptor in read_json(\"index.json\").get(\"manifests\", []):\n            visit(descriptor)\n        return {\"retained\": bool(found), \"reason\": \"Inspected reachable OCI manifests and predicates\",\n                \"attestation_manifests\": found}\n\n\nclass Runner:\n    def __init__(self, out):\n        self.out = out\n\n    def __call__(self, command, *, cwd=None, env=None, stdout_path=None, capture=True):\n        # Spool process output to files: full compiler logs never accumulate in RAM.\n        with tempfile.TemporaryFile(dir=self.out) as stdout, tempfile.TemporaryFile(dir=self.out) as stderr:\n            result = subprocess.run(command, cwd=cwd, env=env, stdout=stdout, stderr=stderr)\n            stdout.seek(0)\n            stderr.seek(0)\n            with (self.out / \"build.stdout\").open(\"ab\") as log:\n                if stdout_path:\n                    with Path(stdout_path).open(\"wb\") as target:\n                        copy_stream(stdout, target)\n                else:\n                    copy_stream(stdout, log)\n            with (self.out / \"build.stderr\").open(\"ab\") as log:\n                copy_stream(stderr, log)\n            if result.returncode:\n                raise RuntimeError(f\"Command exited {result.returncode}: {command!r}\")\n            if stdout_path or not capture:\n                return \"\"\n            stdout.seek(0)\n            return stdout.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n\n\ndef copy_stream(source, target):\n    for chunk in iter(lambda: source.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n        target.write(chunk)\n\n\ndef resolve_base(run, value, kind):\n    expected = f\"nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-{kind}-ubuntu24.04\"\n    name, separator, digest = value.partition(\"@\")\n    if name not in (expected, \"docker.io/\" + expected):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Expected {expected}, got {name}\")\n    if not separator:\n        info = json.loads(run([\"docker\", \"image\", \"inspect\", name]))[0]\n        candidates = [item.partition(\"@\")[2] for item in info.get(\"RepoDigests\", [])\n                      if item.partition(\"@\")[0] in (\"nvidia/cuda\", \"docker.io/nvidia/cuda\")]\n        if not candidates:\n            raise ValueError(f\"No local RepoDigest for {name}; set BASE_{kind.upper()}=name@sha256:...\")\n        digest = candidates[0]\n    if not re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", digest):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid base digest: \" + digest)\n    return {\"reference\": name + \"@\" + digest, \"digest\": digest}\n\n\ndef build(args, runner=None):\n    out = Path(args.out).resolve()\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    # Never overwrite evidence from an earlier attempt.\n    if any(out.iterdir()):\n        raise ValueError(\"--out must be an empty directory\")\n    for name in (\"build.stdout\", \"build.stderr\"):\n        (out / name).touch()\n    run = runner or Runner(out)\n    started = time.monotonic()\n    record = {\n        \"schema_version\": 1, \"status\": \"failed\", \"failure_stage\": None,\n        \"started_at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n        \"source\": {\"path\": str(Path(args.source).resolve()), \"requested_commit\": args.commit,\n                   \"commit\": None, \"tree\": None, \"dirty\": None, \"status_porcelain\": None},\n        \"patch_sha256\": None, \"extra_targets\": list(getattr(args, \"extra_target\", []) or []), \"tag\": args.tag, \"platform\": \"linux/amd64\",\n        \"cmake_flags\": CMAKE_FLAGS,\n        \"recipes\": {}, \"base_images\": {}, \"versions\": {},\n        \"image\": None, \"tools\": {}, \"app_files\": {}, \"archive\": None, \"buildx_metadata\": None,\n        \"provenance\": {\"retained\": False, \"reason\": \"Archive not inspected\"},\n        \"build_wall_seconds\": None,\n    }\n    stage = \"recipes\"\n    try:\n        record[\"recipes\"] = {name: file_digest(RECIPES / name)\n                             for name in (\"Dockerfile\", \"docker-bake.hcl\")}\n        stage = \"verify_source\"\n        source = Path(args.source).resolve()\n        git_env = os.environ.copy()\n        git_env[\"GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS\"] = \"0\"\n\n        def git(*items):\n            return run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(source), *items], env=git_env).strip()\n\n        if not re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-fA-F]{7,40}\", args.commit):\n            raise ValueError(\"--commit must be a hexadecimal SHA (7-40 characters)\")\n        if Path(git(\"rev-parse\", \"--show-toplevel\")).resolve() != source:\n            raise ValueError(\"--source must be the checkout root\")\n        head = git(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n        expected = git(\"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", args.commit + \"^{commit}\")\n        record[\"source\"].update(commit=head, tree=git(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD^{tree}\"))\n        dirty = git(\"status\", \"--porcelain=v1\", \"--untracked-files=all\")\n        record[\"source\"].update(dirty=bool(dirty), status_porcelain=dirty)\n        if head != expected:\n            raise ValueError(\"Source HEAD does not match --commit\")\n        if dirty:\n            raise ValueError(\"Source is dirty; commit changes or supply --patch\")\n        if any(line.startswith(\"160000 \") for line in git(\"ls-files\", \"--stage\").splitlines()):\n            raise ValueError(\"Submodules are unsupported; git archive would omit their contents\")\n\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"staging-\", dir=out) as temporary:\n            temporary = Path(temporary)\n            stage = \"stage_source\"\n            snapshot = temporary / \"source.tar\"\n            run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(source), \"archive\", \"--format=tar\", head],\n                env=git_env, stdout_path=snapshot)\n            staged = temporary / \"source\"\n            staged.mkdir()\n            with tarfile.open(snapshot) as archive:\n                archive.extractall(staged, filter=\"data\")\n            if args.patch:\n                stage = \"patch_check\"\n                patch = temporary / \"input.patch\"\n                patch.write_bytes(Path(args.patch).read_bytes())\n                record[\"patch_sha256\"] = file_digest(patch)[\"sha256\"]\n                patch_env = git_env.copy()\n                patch_env[\"GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES\"] = str(temporary)\n                run([\"git\", \"apply\", \"--check\", str(patch)], cwd=staged, env=patch_env)\n                stage = \"patch_apply\"\n                run([\"git\", \"apply\", str(patch)], cwd=staged, env=patch_env)\n            # User-supplied ignore rules must not silently remove tracked source.\n            for ignore in (\".dockerignore\", \"Dockerfile.dockerignore\"):\n                ignore_path = staged / ignore\n                if ignore_path.is_symlink():\n                    ignore_path.unlink()\n                ignore_path.write_text(\"\")\n\n            stage = \"versions\"\n            record[\"versions\"][\"docker\"] = run([\"docker\", \"version\", \"--format\", \"{{json .}}\"])\n            record[\"versions\"][\"buildx\"] = run([\"docker\", \"buildx\", \"version\"]).strip()\n            stage = \"base_images\"\n            record[\"base_images\"][\"devel\"] = resolve_base(\n                run, os.environ.get(\"BASE_DEVEL\", DEFAULT_DEVEL), \"devel\")\n            record[\"base_images\"][\"runtime\"] = resolve_base(\n                run, os.environ.get(\"BASE_RUNTIME\", DEFAULT_RUNTIME), \"runtime\")\n            env = os.environ.copy()\n            env.update(TAG=args.tag, SOURCE_DIR=str(staged), SOURCE_COMMIT=head, EXTRA_TARGETS=\" \".join(getattr(args, \"extra_target\", []) or []),\n                       PATCH_SHA256=record[\"patch_sha256\"] or \"\",\n                       BASE_DEVEL=record[\"base_images\"][\"devel\"][\"reference\"],\n                       BASE_RUNTIME=record[\"base_images\"][\"runtime\"][\"reference\"],\n                       BUILDX_METADATA_PROVENANCE=\"max\")\n            stage = \"build\"\n            build_started = time.monotonic()\n            try:\n                # Stage the recipe INSIDE the build context so Bake needs no filesystem entitlements (no fs.read=/).\n                recipe_dir = staged / \".campaign-recipe\"; recipe_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n                for name in (\"Dockerfile\", \"docker-bake.hcl\"):\n                    shutil.copy2(RECIPES / name, recipe_dir / name)\n                env[\"SOURCE_DIR\"] = \".\"\n                run([\"docker\", \"buildx\", \"bake\", \"--file\", str(recipe_dir / \"docker-bake.hcl\"),\n                     \"--metadata-file\", str(out / \"buildx-metadata.json\"), \"--progress\", \"plain\", \"engine\"],\n                    cwd=staged, env=env, capture=False)\n            finally:\n                record[\"build_wall_seconds\"] = time.monotonic() - build_started\n                if (out / \"buildx-metadata.json\").exists():\n                    record[\"buildx_metadata\"] = json.loads((out / \"buildx-metadata.json\").read_text())\n\n        stage = \"inspect_image\"\n        info = json.loads(run([\"docker\", \"image\", \"inspect\", args.tag]))[0]\n        record[\"image\"] = {key: info.get(key) for key in\n                           (\"Id\", \"RepoDigests\", \"Created\", \"Architecture\", \"Os\")}\n        if info.get(\"Architecture\") != \"amd64\" or info.get(\"Os\") != \"linux\":\n            raise ValueError(\"Built image is not linux/amd64\")\n        # Use the immutable config ID after resolving the tag exactly once.\n        image_id = info[\"Id\"]\n        stage = \"hash_tools\"\n        hashes = run([\"docker\", \"run\", \"--rm\", \"--network=none\", \"--read-only\",\n                      \"--entrypoint\", \"/bin/sh\", image_id, \"-c\",\n                      \"find /app -type f -print0 | sort -z | xargs -0 /usr/bin/sha256sum\"])\n        for line in hashes.splitlines():\n            digest, name = line.split(maxsplit=1)\n            if not re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", digest):\n                raise ValueError(\"Invalid file sha256\")\n            record[\"app_files\"][name.strip()] = digest   # every regular file shipped in /app (binaries AND shared libraries)\n        required = {\"/app/\" + tool for tool in TOOLS + tuple(getattr(args, \"extra_target\", []) or [])}\n        if not required <= set(record[\"app_files\"]):\n            raise ValueError(\"Missing tool hashes: \" + \", \".join(sorted(required - set(record[\"app_files\"]))))\n        record[\"tools\"] = {k: v for k, v in record[\"app_files\"].items() if k in required}\n        stage = \"save_image\"\n        image_tar = out / \"engine-image.docker.tar\"\n        run([\"docker\", \"save\", \"--output\", str(image_tar), image_id])\n        record[\"archive\"] = {\"path\": image_tar.name, **file_digest(image_tar)}\n        record[\"image\"].update({\"docker_reported_id\": info[\"Id\"], **{\"config_digest\": None, \"index_digest\": None}})\n        ids = archive_identities(image_tar)\n        record[\"image\"][\"config_digest\"], record[\"image\"][\"index_digest\"] = ids[\"config_digest\"], ids[\"index_digest\"]\n        record[\"image\"][\"index_manifests\"] = ids[\"index_manifests\"]\n        record[\"image\"][\"docker_id_in_archive_index\"] = info[\"Id\"] in ids.get(\"index_entry_digests\", [])\n        record[\"image\"][\"id_note\"] = \"Id/docker_reported_id is whatever `docker image inspect` returned (containerd store: an index digest). config_digest is the image config digest. They are different objects.\"\n        stage = \"inspect_provenance\"\n        record[\"provenance\"] = archive_provenance(image_tar)\n        record.update(status=\"success\", failure_stage=None)\n    except Exception as exc:\n        record.update(status=\"failed\", failure_stage=stage, error=str(exc))\n        with (out / \"build.stderr\").open(\"a\") as log:\n            log.write(f\"\\n{stage}: {exc}\\n\")\n    finally:\n        record[\"wall_seconds\"] = time.monotonic() - started\n        record[\"finished_at\"] = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n        (out / \"build-record.json\").write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return 0 if record[\"status\"] == \"success\" else 1\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--source\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--commit\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--patch\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--extra-target\", action=\"append\", default=[], help=\"extra CMake executable target to build and ship in /app (e.g. llama-routing-trace added by a patch)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--tag\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    try:\n        return build(args)\n    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n        parser.exit(1, str(exc) + \"\\n\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n\"\"\"No Docker daemon, CUDA toolkit, GPU, or network needed.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport io\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tarfile\n\nimport pytest\n\nimport build_engine as engine\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef source(tmp_path):\n    repo = tmp_path / \"repo\"\n    repo.mkdir()\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"init\", \"--quiet\", str(repo)], check=True)\n    (repo / \"input.txt\").write_text(\"original\\n\")\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(repo), \"add\", \".\"], check=True)\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(repo), \"-c\", \"user.name=Test\", \"-c\",\n                    \"user.email=test@example.invalid\", \"-c\", \"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\",\n                    \"commit\", \"--quiet\", \"-m\", \"fixture\"], check=True)\n    return repo\n\n\ndef arguments(source, tmp_path, patch=None):\n    commit = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"-C\", str(source), \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], text=True).strip()\n    return argparse.Namespace(source=str(source), commit=commit, patch=patch,\n                              tag=\"campaign/test:unit\", out=str(tmp_path / \"out\"))\n\n\ndef record(args):\n    return json.loads((Path(args.out) / \"build-record.json\").read_text())\n\n\ndef make_tar(path, objects):\n    with tarfile.open(path, \"w\") as archive:\n        for name, obj in objects.items():\n            data = json.dumps(obj).encode()\n            member = tarfile.TarInfo(name)\n            member.size = len(data)\n            archive.addfile(member, io.BytesIO(data))\n\n\ndef test_sha256_bytes(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"payload\"\n    data = b\"hello\\x00world\" * 200000\n    path.write_bytes(data)\n    assert engine.file_digest(path) == {\"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), \"bytes\": len(data)}\n    path.write_bytes(b\"\")\n    assert engine.file_digest(path) == {\"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(b\"\").hexdigest(), \"bytes\": 0}\n\n\ndef test_patch_check_failure(source, tmp_path):\n    patch = tmp_path / \"bad.patch\"\n    patch.write_text(\"diff --git a/input.txt b/input.txt\\n--- a/input.txt\\n+++ b/input.txt\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-missing\\n+changed\\n\")\n    args = arguments(source, tmp_path, str(patch))\n    assert engine.build(args) == 1\n    result = record(args)\n    assert result[\"failure_stage\"] == \"patch_check\"\n    assert result[\"patch_sha256\"] == engine.file_digest(patch)[\"sha256\"]\n    assert result[\"source\"][\"dirty\"] is False\n    assert (source / \"input.txt\").read_text() == \"original\\n\"\n    assert \"patch failed\" in (Path(args.out) / \"build.stderr\").read_text()\n    assert (Path(args.out) / \"build.stdout\").exists()\n    assert not list(Path(args.out).glob(\"staging-*\"))\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef mock_docker(monkeypatch):\n    real_run = subprocess.run\n    calls = []\n    state = {\"fail_build\": False, \"staged_content\": None}\n\n    def fake(command, **kwargs):\n        if command[0] != \"docker\":\n            return real_run(command, **kwargs)\n        calls.append(command)\n        stdout, stderr = kwargs[\"stdout\"], kwargs[\"stderr\"]\n        result = \"\"\n        code = 0\n        if command[1] == \"version\":\n            result = '{\"Client\":{\"Version\":\"test\"},\"Server\":{\"Version\":\"test\"}}'\n        elif command[1:3] == [\"buildx\", \"version\"]:\n            result = \"buildx unit-test\"\n        elif command[1:3] == [\"buildx\", \"bake\"]:\n            env = kwargs[\"env\"]\n            staged = Path(kwargs[\"cwd\"])\n            assert env[\"SOURCE_DIR\"] == \".\"\n            assert (staged / \".campaign-recipe\" / \"Dockerfile\").exists()\n            assert Path(command[command.index(\"--file\") + 1]).parent == staged / \".campaign-recipe\"\n            assert not any(a.startswith(\"--allow\") for a in command)  # no filesystem entitlements requested\n            state[\"staged_content\"] = (staged / \"input.txt\").read_text()\n            assert not (staged / \".git\").exists()\n            assert \"@sha256:\" in env[\"BASE_RUNTIME\"]\n            result = \"full compiler stdout\\n\"\n            stderr.write(b\"full compiler stderr\\n\")\n            metadata = {\"engine\": {\"containerimage.config.digest\": \"sha256:\" + \"1\" * 64}}\n            Path(command[command.index(\"--metadata-file\") + 1]).write_text(json.dumps(metadata))\n            code = 42 if state[\"fail_build\"] else 0\n        elif command[1:3] == [\"image\", \"inspect\"]:\n            if command[-1].startswith(\"nvidia/\"):\n                result = json.dumps([{\"RepoDigests\": [\"nvidia/cuda@sha256:\" + \"2\" * 64]}])\n            else:\n                result = json.dumps([{\"Id\": \"sha256:\" + \"1\" * 64, \"RepoDigests\": [],\n                                      \"Created\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\", \"Architecture\": \"amd64\", \"Os\": \"linux\"}])\n        elif command[1] == \"run\":\n            assert \"--network=none\" in command\n            assert \"--rm\" in command\n            assert \"/bin/sh\" in command and \"sha256sum\" in command[-1]\n            assert \"sha256:\" + \"1\" * 64 in command   # hashed by immutable id, not by tag\n            result = \"\".join(\"a\" * 64 + \"  /app/\" + tool + \"\\n\" for tool in engine.TOOLS) + \"b\" * 64 + \"  /app/libggml.so.0\\n\"\n        elif command[1] == \"save\":\n            assert command[-1] == \"sha256:\" + \"1\" * 64\n            make_tar(command[command.index(\"--output\") + 1], {\"manifest.json\": []})\n        else:\n            pytest.fail(\"Unexpected Docker command: \" + repr(command))\n        stdout.write(result.encode())\n        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(command, code)\n\n    monkeypatch.delenv(\"BASE_DEVEL\", raising=False)\n    monkeypatch.delenv(\"BASE_RUNTIME\", raising=False)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(subprocess, \"run\", fake)\n    return calls, state\n\n\ndef test_record_schema_and_success(source, tmp_path, mock_docker):\n    args = arguments(source, tmp_path)\n    assert engine.build(args) == 0\n    result = record(args)\n    assert result[\"schema_version\"] == 1\n    assert result[\"status\"] == \"success\"\n    assert result[\"failure_stage\"] is None\n    assert result[\"source\"][\"commit\"] == args.commit\n    assert len(result[\"source\"][\"tree\"]) == 40\n    assert result[\"source\"][\"dirty\"] is False\n    assert result[\"patch_sha256\"] is None\n    assert result[\"platform\"] == \"linux/amd64\"\n    assert result[\"cmake_flags\"] == engine.CMAKE_FLAGS\n    assert {\"Id\", \"RepoDigests\", \"Created\", \"Architecture\", \"Os\", \"docker_reported_id\", \"config_digest\", \"index_digest\"} <= set(result[\"image\"])\n    assert set(result[\"tools\"]) == {\"/app/\" + tool for tool in engine.TOOLS}\n    assert \"/app/libggml.so.0\" in result[\"app_files\"] and \"/app/libggml.so.0\" not in result[\"tools\"]   # libraries hashed too\n    # identities are distinct objects: the record must not present the docker-reported Id as the config digest\n    assert result[\"image\"][\"docker_reported_id\"] == result[\"image\"][\"Id\"]\n    assert result[\"archive\"][\"sha256\"] == engine.file_digest(Path(args.out) / result[\"archive\"][\"path\"])[\"sha256\"]\n    assert result[\"archive\"][\"bytes\"] > 0\n    assert result[\"base_images\"][\"runtime\"][\"digest\"] == \"sha256:\" + \"2\" * 64\n    assert set(result[\"versions\"]) == {\"docker\", \"buildx\"}\n    assert result[\"buildx_metadata\"][\"engine\"]\n    assert result[\"build_wall_seconds\"] >= 0\n    assert result[\"wall_seconds\"] >= result[\"build_wall_seconds\"]\n    assert result[\"provenance\"][\"retained\"] is False\n    assert \"full compiler stdout\" in (Path(args.out) / \"build.stdout\").read_text()\n    assert \"full compiler stderr\" in (Path(args.out) / \"build.stderr\").read_text()\n    calls, _ = mock_docker\n    assert not any(\"--push\" in command or \"prune\" in command for command in calls)\n\n\ndef test_build_failure_preserves_logs_and_metadata(source, tmp_path, mock_docker):\n    mock_docker[1][\"fail_build\"] = True\n    args = arguments(source, tmp_path)\n    assert engine.build(args) == 1\n    result = record(args)\n    assert result[\"failure_stage\"] == \"build\"\n    assert result[\"status\"] == \"failed\"\n    assert result[\"buildx_metadata\"]\n    assert result[\"build_wall_seconds\"] >= 0\n    assert \"full compiler stdout\" in (Path(args.out) / \"build.stdout\").read_text()\n    assert \"full compiler stderr\" in (Path(args.out) / \"build.stderr\").read_text()\n    assert not any(command[1] == \"save\" for command in mock_docker[0])\n\n\ndef test_valid_patch_changes_staging_only(source, tmp_path, mock_docker):\n    patch = tmp_path / \"good.patch\"\n    patch.write_text(\"diff --git a/input.txt b/input.txt\\n--- a/input.txt\\n+++ b/input.txt\\n@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-original\\n+changed\\n\")\n    args = arguments(source, tmp_path, str(patch))\n    assert engine.build(args) == 0\n    assert mock_docker[1][\"staged_content\"] == \"changed\\n\"\n    assert (source / \"input.txt\").read_text() == \"original\\n\"\n    assert record(args)[\"patch_sha256\"] == engine.file_digest(patch)[\"sha256\"]\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"change\", [\"dirty\", \"wrong_commit\"])\ndef test_source_rejected(source, tmp_path, change):\n    args = arguments(source, tmp_path)\n    if change == \"dirty\":\n        (source / \"input.txt\").write_text(\"dirty\\n\")\n    else:\n        args.commit = \"0\" * 40\n    assert engine.build(args) == 1\n    assert record(args)[\"failure_stage\"] == \"verify_source\"\n    if change == \"dirty\":\n        assert record(args)[\"source\"][\"dirty\"] is True\n\n\ndef test_runner_captures_stdout_stderr_on_error(tmp_path):\n    for name in (\"build.stdout\", \"build.stderr\"):\n        (tmp_path / name).touch()\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError):\n        engine.Runner(tmp_path)([sys.executable, \"-c\",\n                                \"import sys; print('out'); print('err', file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(9)\"])\n    assert (tmp_path / \"build.stdout\").read_text() == \"out\\n\"\n    assert (tmp_path / \"build.stderr\").read_text() == \"err\\n\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"predicate,retained\", [\n    (\"https://slsa.dev/provenance/v0.2\", True),\n    (\"https://spdx.dev/Document\", False),\n])\ndef test_oci_provenance_requires_actual_predicate(tmp_path, predicate, retained):\n    path = tmp_path / \"oci.tar\"\n    manifest_digest, layer_digest = \"3\" * 64, \"4\" * 64\n    make_tar(path, {\n        \"index.json\": {\"manifests\": [{\"digest\": \"sha256:\" + manifest_digest,\n                        \"annotations\": {\"vnd.docker.reference.type\": \"attestation-manifest\"}}]},\n        \"blobs/sha256/\" + manifest_digest: {\"layers\": [{\"mediaType\": \"application/vnd.in-toto+json\",\n                                                          \"digest\": \"sha256:\" + layer_digest}]},\n        \"blobs/sha256/\" + layer_digest: {\"predicateType\": predicate},\n    })\n    assert engine.archive_provenance(path)[\"retained\"] is retained\n\n\ndef test_empty_output_required(source, tmp_path):\n    args = arguments(source, tmp_path)\n    out = Path(args.out)\n    out.mkdir()\n    (out / \"build-record.json\").write_text(\"keep\")\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"empty\"):\n        engine.build(args)\n    assert (out / \"build-record.json\").read_text() == \"keep\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short\ncat cc/gpu_budget/README.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short\ncat cc/gpu_budget/README.md'","aggregated_output":" M evidence/claude-code.jsonl\n?? artifacts/codexM/\n?? artifacts/codexN/\n?? artifacts/codexO/\n?? artifacts/codexP/\n?? artifacts/op-5b2c76785e3c/\n?? artifacts/op-8a2b0f459ce8/\n?? artifacts/op-9bd00d8d51d1/\n?? artifacts/op-b4a6fa6e3d57/\n?? artifacts/op-caf6d1ec344c/\n?? artifacts/op-ccc639ba92d1/\n?? artifacts/x3-shim/\n?? assignments/T-M-runner-bytes.md\n?? assignments/T-N-build-cmake-flags.md\n?? assignments/T-O-static-hot-experts.md\n?? assignments/T-P-resource-observe.md\n?? evidence/codex-M.jsonl\n?? evidence/codex-N.jsonl\n?? evidence/codex-O.jsonl\n?? evidence/codex-P.jsonl\n# GPU allocation budget shim\n\n`libgpubudget.so` is a process-local `LD_PRELOAD` interposer for Linux and CUDA\n12.8. It caps **successful, intercepted allocation sizes**, aggregated across\nall devices and contexts in one process. It requires no driver changes, MPS,\nnetwork access, or privileged container options. It is an experiment control,\nnot a security boundary or a limit on physical VRAM reported by `nvidia-smi`.\n\nThe assignment's approximate scale is `128/500 * 2.67 GiB ≈ 700 MiB`.\nSet `GPU_BUDGET_MIB=700` for that allocation budget. If the 2.67 GB figure uses\ndecimal units instead, the corresponding result is approximately 652 MiB;\n700 MiB is the requested campaign approximation.\n\n## Build and test (orchestrator)\n\nRun these from the campaign root. These are instructions for the orchestrator;\nthe authoring agent did not run Docker. The source mount is read-only and all\ncompiler outputs go into the separate writable output mount:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p artifacts/codexL/cuda\ndocker run --rm --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\" \\\n  -v \"$PWD/cc/gpu_budget:/src:ro\" \\\n  -v \"$PWD/artifacts/codexL/cuda:/out\" \\\n  campaign/cuda-tools:c1 bash /src/build.sh /out\n\ndocker run --rm --gpus all --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\" \\\n  -v \"$PWD/cc/gpu_budget:/src:ro\" \\\n  -v \"$PWD/artifacts/codexL/cuda:/out\" \\\n  campaign/cuda-tools:c1 bash /src/run_test.sh /out\n```\n\n`build.sh [output-dir]` is the single build command inside the image. It uses\n`gcc` and CUDA headers for the shim, then `nvcc --cudart shared` for the test.\nThe shim depends only on the ELF loader, libc, and pthreads; it does not link\nagainst CUDA libraries. The test links the CUDA driver stub at build time,\nwithout embedding the stub directory in its runtime search path. At execution,\nthe NVIDIA container runtime must supply the real `libcuda.so.1`.\n\n`run_test.sh` pins budget=250, reserve=0, managed counting=1. It prints a\nPASS/FAIL table and exits nonzero if any check fails. It checks 3 × 100 MiB,\nthird-allocation OOM, free/reuse, exact memory-info values, async allocation,\nasync denial/free/reuse, pitched/3D/managed accounting, and direct synchronous\nand asynchronous driver allocation. It writes `test-budget.jsonl` in the output\ndirectory unless `GPU_BUDGET_LOG` is supplied. A GPU with managed memory and\nCUDA memory-pool support is required; unsupported async APIs are explicit test\nfailures, not silent passes.\n\n## Using with the engine\n\nSet `ENGINE_DIR` to the Build CC build output containing `bin/llama-cli` and\n`MODEL_DIR` to the model directory. For example:\n\n```bash\ndocker run --rm --gpus all \\\n  -v \"$ENGINE_DIR:/engine:ro\" \\\n  -v \"$MODEL_DIR:/models:ro\" \\\n  -v \"$PWD/artifacts/codexL/cuda:/budget:ro\" \\\n  -v \"$PWD/artifacts/codexL:/logs\" \\\n  -e LD_PRELOAD=/budget/libgpubudget.so \\\n  -e GPU_BUDGET_MIB=700 \\\n  -e GPU_BUDGET_LOG=/logs/engine-budget.jsonl \\\n  -e GGML_CUDA_NO_VMM=1 \\\n  campaign/cuda-tools:c1 \\\n  /engine/bin/llama-cli -m /models/model.gguf -ngl 999 -p 'Hello'\n```\n\n**VMM must actually be disabled in the engine build.** Source inspection of\nthis checkout found `GGML_CUDA_NO_VMM` is a compile-time setting, not a runtime\nenvironment switch. The environment setting above expresses the requested\ncampaign intent, but by itself has **no effect** on this revision. Build CC\nmust configure llama.cpp with `-DGGML_CUDA_NO_VMM=ON` and rebuild its CUDA backend.\n`ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh:232` and `CMakeLists.txt:147` guard VMM at compile\ntime; `ggml-cuda.cu:725` otherwise chooses the VMM pool when supported.\nCheck the Build CC `CMakeCache.txt` for `GGML_CUDA_NO_VMM:BOOL=ON`, the backend\nfeature report for `NO_VMM = 1`, and confirm budget-log `cudaMalloc` allocation\nevents while loading the model. A device capability line saying `VMM: yes`\nalone does not prove which pool was selected.\n\nThis requires dynamically linked CUDA runtime calls. The campaign image is\nspecified to link `libggml-cuda.so` against `libcudart.so.12`; verify the actual\nBuild CC artifact inside the image with `ldd /engine/bin/libggml-cuda.so` (adjust\nthe path if needed). Inspect `readelf -Ws` for undefined `cudaMalloc` and check\nthat the engine produces allocation events in the budget log. Static cudart,\nprivate symbol lookup, or direct driver function pointers can bypass preload.\nThe image and engine binary were unavailable for execution in this workspace,\nso their dynamic linkage and actual pool selection have not been GPU-verified.\n\nEngines using `cudaMemGetInfo`/`cuMemGetInfo_v2` or llama.cpp's\n`ggml_backend_dev_memory` see the synthetic budget and free balance. Fit logic\ncan reduce GPU layers or offload to CPU. Allocators that do not adapt receive\nOOM and may abort; llama.cpp pool growth, temporary buffers, and KV cache also\nconsume this budget. An exact physical-memory simulation is not implied.\n\n## Configuration and accounting\n\n| Variable | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `GPU_BUDGET_MIB` | Unsigned integer binary MiB. Absent: no cap and real memory-info values. `0`: no positive-size allocations. |\n| `GPU_BUDGET_RESERVE_MIB` | Default 0. Effective allocation capacity is `max(budget - reserve, 0)`. |\n| `GPU_BUDGET_COUNT_MANAGED` | `1` (default): charge requested managed bytes immediately, without tracking residency/prefetch. `0`: managed memory is outside the budget. |\n| `GPU_BUDGET_LOG` | Optional writable JSONL path, opened in append mode. All events are flushed immediately, including denials, plus a final summary at normal exit/unload. |\n\nConfiguration is read once on first intercepted outer call. Malformed integers,\noverflow, invalid managed settings, or an unopenable requested log terminate\nwith exit 125 rather than silently dropping the restriction. Each process has\nits own cap and must have its own log path for unambiguous records.\n\n`cudaMemGetInfo` and `cuMemGetInfo_v2` first invoke the real API so normal\ninitialization and invalid-argument/context errors are preserved. After success,\n`total = budget`, `free = max(budget - reserve, 0) - used`. Allocation accounting\nuses successful requested bytes, with padding included for pitched storage.\nNo allocation is issued when that amount exceeds the remaining capacity.\nUnderlying CUDA allocation failures leave the counter unchanged. Denials return\n`cudaErrorMemoryAllocation` or `CUDA_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY`; output arguments on\nfailure must not be used. A missing real entry point returns NOT_SUPPORTED.\nSynthetic failures return the specified error directly; they do not update\ncudart's private last-error state for `cudaGetLastError`/`cudaPeekAtLastError`.\n\nA mutex serializes decisions, real calls, and pointer-hash-table updates. A\nthread-local nesting guard prevents runtime→driver calls from charging twice.\nBookkeeping storage is reserved before invoking an allocator; metadata OOM is\nalso an allocation denial. Successful frees of unknown pointers are passed\nthrough and do not change the balance. Failed frees retain their charge.\n\n`cudaFreeAsync` and `cuMemFreeAsync` **synchronize their stream after enqueueing\nthe free** before returning budget to the counter. They therefore block and\nalter async performance/ordering. Stream synchronization errors retain the\ncharge conservatively, even if the underlying free eventually completes; the\nbalance may stay lower until process exit. No event polling or background\nreaper is used. Async allocation is charged immediately on successful enqueue.\n\n`cudaMallocPitch` and `cudaMalloc3D`, while the cap is enabled, synthesize linear\nstorage through real `cudaMalloc`. Pitch is rounded to at least 512 bytes and\nthe device's texture and texture-pitch alignments, and checked against maximum\npitch. The charged size is `pitch * height [* depth]`, checked for overflow.\nReturned `xsize`/`ysize` retain requested extents. This avoids speculative\nover-budget allocations, but pitch can differ from native cudart. Pitched\nallocation with zero extents is rejected. Texture-specific uses and exact\nnative pitch compatibility require validation on the target GPU; the intended\nllama.cpp path uses ordinary `cudaMalloc`.\n\nThe JSONL fields are `event`, `api`, `pointer` (hex string), `bytes`, `used`,\n`peak`, `budget`, `reserve`, `capacity`, and numeric `status`. Events are\n`init`, `alloc`, `free`, `deny`, `error`, and `exit`. `used`/`peak` exclude the\nreserve. Opted-out managed allocations still log their requested size without\nchanging counters; their frees are unknown-size (`bytes=0`) events.\nNo summary is guaranteed for SIGKILL, `_exit`, or fatal crashes;\nalready-flushed events survive. Atexit and destructor share an idempotent\nfinalizer, so ordinary exit logs the summary once.\n\n## Coverage and limitations\n\nCovered exported symbols:\n\n| API family | Symbols |\n| --- | --- |\n| Runtime allocation | `cudaMalloc`, `cudaMallocAsync`, `cudaMallocPitch`, `cudaMalloc3D`, `cudaMallocManaged` |\n| Runtime free/info | `cudaFree`, `cudaFreeAsync`, `cudaMemGetInfo` |\n| Driver allocation | `cuMemAlloc_v2`, `cuMemAllocAsync` |\n| Driver free/info | `cuMemFree_v2`, `cuMemFreeAsync`, `cuMemGetInfo_v2` |\n\n**Not covered:** `cuMemCreate` / `cuMemRelease` and VMM mappings; arrays and\nmipmapped arrays; `cuMemAllocManaged`, driver pitched allocation, explicit\n`*FromPoolAsync`; IPC/imported/external allocations; host allocation/mapping\n(`cudaHostAlloc`, `cudaHostRegister`, mapped host memory); per-thread-default-\nstream `_ptsz` symbols and legacy unversioned driver ABI symbols; direct\n`cuGetProcAddress`/`cudaGetDriverEntryPoint` lookups; deep-bound or statically\nlinked CUDA; and allocation/context cleanup through `cudaDeviceReset` or\ncontext destruction. Do not reset/destroy contexts while tracked allocations\nremain live. Start a new process between trials. Forking after CUDA/shim\ninitialization and CUDA graph capture/replay are unsupported.\n\nVMM is deliberately left unsupported: releasing a generic allocation handle\ndoes **not** release physical storage while mappings survive. This checkout's\nllama.cpp maps each allocation then immediately calls `cuMemRelease`, so a\nsimple handle-only wrapper would falsely restore the budget. Correct coverage\nwould also require mapping lifetimes, aliases, imports, retained handles, and\npartial unmaps. Until that exists, build with VMM disabled as described above.\n\nCUDA context/cuBLAS workspace overhead (approximately 300 MiB, device and\nversion dependent), internal driver/cudart allocations, kernels' local memory,\nallocation granularity, and pool caches/reserved memory are **not counted**.\nPools may retain physical memory after a charged logical allocation is freed.\nTo leave room for estimated overhead within a 700 MiB experiment envelope, use\n`GPU_BUDGET_MIB=700 GPU_BUDGET_RESERVE_MIB=300`: total reports 700 MiB and initial\nfree is 400 MiB. If 700 MiB should be available specifically to intercepted\nallocations, leave reserve at 0 and allow overhead outside that amount.\nMeasure the real overhead separately; the reserve is an estimate, not telemetry.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\nNo network or Docker was used. CUDA headers, nvcc, and a GPU runtime were not\navailable on the authoring host. The complete test program passed against a\nCPU-only fake CUDA backend, which uses actual ELF preload and deliberately\nnests runtime→driver calls. Additional checks cover 16 concurrent allocators,\nbackend allocation failures, unknown/null frees, overflow, reserve, managed\nopt-out, sync failure, zero/disabled caps, invalid configuration, and JSONL\ninvariants. See `artifacts/codexL/host-verification.txt` and reproduce with\n`bash artifacts/codexL/host_mock/verify.sh`. These mocks are not CUDA ABI or\nGPU correctness evidence. The orchestrator must still run the build and real\nCUDA tests above, then validate the actual Build CC engine under the shim.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
