{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' cc/build_engine/build_engine.py\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Build a local CUDA engine and record evidence; uses only the Python stdlib.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport shutil\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport tarfile\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nRECIPES = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / \"recipes\"\nTOOLS = (\"llama-bench\", \"llama-perplexity\", \"llama-completion\", \"llama-server\",\n         \"llama-eval-callback\", \"llama-cli\", \"llama-tokenize\")\nCMAKE_FLAGS = [\"-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\", \"-DGGML_CUDA=ON\",\n               \"-DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=120\", \"-DLLAMA_CURL=OFF\",\n               \"-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON\", \"-DGGML_NATIVE=OFF\",\n               \"-DLLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=OFF\", \"-DLLAMA_BUILD_UI=OFF\",\n               \"-DLLAMA_USE_PREBUILT_UI=OFF\", \"-DLLAMA_OPENSSL=OFF\",\n               \"-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache\", \"-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache\",\n               \"-DCMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache\",\n               \"-DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS=-Wl,--allow-shlib-undefined\"]\nDEFAULT_DEVEL = (\"nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-devel-ubuntu24.04@sha256:\"\n                 \"520292dbb4f755fd360766059e62956e9379485d9e073bbd2f6e3c20c270ed66\")\nDEFAULT_RUNTIME = \"nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-runtime-ubuntu24.04\"\n\n\ndef validate_defines(items):\n    \"\"\"Return canonical definitions; allow only literal, single shell words.\"\"\"\n    builtins = {flag[2:].split(\"=\", 1)[0] for flag in CMAKE_FLAGS}\n    defines = {}\n    for item in items:\n        key, separator, value = item.partition(\"=\")\n        if not separator or not re.fullmatch(r\"[A-Z0-9_]+\", key):\n            raise ValueError(\"--cmake-define requires KEY=VALUE with KEY matching ^[A-Z0-9_]+$\")\n        if not re.fullmatch(r\"[A-Za-z0-9_./:+,@%=-]+\", value):\n            raise ValueError(\"--cmake-define VALUE must be nonempty and contain only letters, digits, _./:+,@%=-\")\n        if key in builtins or key in defines:\n            raise ValueError(\"Duplicate or built-in CMake definition: \" + key)\n        defines[key] = value\n    return dict(sorted(defines.items()))\n\n\ndef recipe_identity(defines, extra_targets=()):\n    recipes = {name: file_digest(RECIPES / name)\n               for name in (\"Dockerfile\", \"docker-bake.hcl\")}\n    inputs = {\"recipes\": recipes, \"cmake_defines\": defines,\n              \"cmake_flags\": CMAKE_FLAGS, \"extra_targets\": list(extra_targets)}\n    digest = hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(inputs, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode()).hexdigest()\n    return recipes, digest\n\n\nLINKAGE_SYMBOLS = (\"cudaMalloc\", \"cudaFree\", \"cudaMemGetInfo\")\nLINKAGE_SCRIPT = r'''\nlibrary=\"\"\nfor candidate in /app/libggml-cuda.so /app/libggml-cuda.so.*; do\n    if [ -f \"$candidate\" ]; then library=\"$candidate\"; break; fi\ndone\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_LIBRARY__%s\\n' \"$library\"\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_LDD_BEGIN__\\n'\nif [ -z \"$library\" ]; then\n    echo 'CUDA backend library not found in /app'; ldd_rc=125\nelif command -v ldd >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    ldd \"$library\" 2>&1; ldd_rc=$?\nelse\n    echo 'ldd unavailable in runtime image'; ldd_rc=127\nfi\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_LDD_END__%s\\n' \"$ldd_rc\"\nsymbol_tool=unavailable\nif command -v readelf >/dev/null 2>&1; then symbol_tool=readelf\nelif command -v nm >/dev/null 2>&1; then symbol_tool=nm; fi\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_SYMBOLS_BEGIN__%s\\n' \"$symbol_tool\"\nif [ -z \"$library\" ]; then\n    echo 'CUDA backend library not found in /app'; symbols_rc=125\nelif [ \"$symbol_tool\" = readelf ]; then\n    readelf -Ws \"$library\" 2>&1; symbols_rc=$?\nelif [ \"$symbol_tool\" = nm ]; then\n    nm -D \"$library\" 2>&1; symbols_rc=$?\nelse\n    echo 'readelf and nm unavailable in runtime image'; symbols_rc=127\nfi\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_SYMBOLS_END__%s\\n' \"$symbols_rc\"\n'''\n\n\ndef parse_linkage(ldd_text, symbols_text, *, symbol_tool=\"readelf\",\n                  ldd_returncode=0, symbols_returncode=0):\n    dynamic = None if ldd_returncode else bool(re.search(r\"\\blibcudart\\.so(?:\\.[\\w.]+)?\\b\", ldd_text))\n    imports = {name: None for name in LINKAGE_SYMBOLS}\n    if not symbols_returncode and symbol_tool in (\"readelf\", \"nm\"):\n        for name in imports:\n            if symbol_tool == \"readelf\":\n                pattern = r\"\\bUND\\s+\" + name + r\"(?:@\\S+)?(?:\\s|$)\"\n            else:\n                pattern = r\"^\\s*(?:[0-9a-fA-F]+\\s+)?[Uwv]\\s+\" + name + r\"(?:@\\S+)?(?:\\s|$)\"\n            imports[name] = bool(re.search(pattern, symbols_text, re.MULTILINE))\n    unavailable = bool(ldd_returncode or symbols_returncode or symbol_tool not in (\"readelf\", \"nm\"))\n    passed = dynamic is True and all(value is True for value in imports.values())\n    return {\"status\": \"unavailable\" if unavailable else \"passed\" if passed else \"failed\",\n            \"libcudart_dynamic\": dynamic, \"undefined_imports\": imports,\n            \"ldd\": {\"returncode\": ldd_returncode,\n                    \"reason\": ldd_text.strip() if ldd_returncode else None},\n            \"symbols\": {\"tool\": symbol_tool, \"returncode\": symbols_returncode,\n                        \"reason\": symbols_text.strip() if symbols_returncode or symbol_tool == \"unavailable\" else None}}\n\n\ndef collect_linkage(run, out, image_id):\n    result = {\"status\": \"unavailable\", \"image_config_id\": image_id,\n              \"libcudart_dynamic\": None, \"undefined_imports\": dict.fromkeys(LINKAGE_SYMBOLS),\n              \"raw_output\": \"linkage.raw.txt\"}\n    try:\n        run([\"docker\", \"run\", \"--rm\", \"--network=none\", \"--read-only\",\n             \"--entrypoint\", \"/bin/sh\", image_id, \"-c\", LINKAGE_SCRIPT],\n            stdout_path=out / \"linkage.raw.txt\", stderr_path=out / \"linkage.stderr.txt\", timeout=60)\n        raw = (out / \"linkage.raw.txt\").read_text()\n        match = re.fullmatch(r\"__CAMPAIGN_LIBRARY__([^\\n]*)\\n__CAMPAIGN_LDD_BEGIN__\\n(.*?)\"\n                             r\"__CAMPAIGN_LDD_END__(\\d+)\\n__CAMPAIGN_SYMBOLS_BEGIN__(\\w+)\\n(.*?)\"\n                             r\"__CAMPAIGN_SYMBOLS_END__(\\d+)\\n\", raw, re.DOTALL)\n        if not match:\n            raise ValueError(\"Malformed linkage probe output; see linkage.raw.txt and linkage.stderr.txt\")\n        library, ldd, ldd_rc, tool, symbols, symbols_rc = match.groups()\n        (out / \"linkage.ldd.txt\").write_text(ldd)\n        (out / \"linkage.symbols.txt\").write_text(symbols)\n        result.update(parse_linkage(ldd, symbols, symbol_tool=tool,\n                                   ldd_returncode=int(ldd_rc), symbols_returncode=int(symbols_rc)))\n        result.update(library=library or None, ldd_output=\"linkage.ldd.txt\",\n                      symbols_output=\"linkage.symbols.txt\")\n    except Exception as exc:\n        result.update(status=\"unavailable\", reason=str(exc))\n    return result\n\n\ndef file_digest(path):\n    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n    size = 0\n    with Path(path).open(\"rb\") as stream:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: stream.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n            digest.update(chunk)\n            size += len(chunk)\n    return {\"sha256\": digest.hexdigest(), \"bytes\": size}\n\n\ndef archive_identities(path):\n    \"\"\"Distinct identities from a `docker save` archive: config digest (image config), top-level index digest (what the containerd store\n    reports as `Id`), and image-manifest digests. Never conflate them: only the config digest is the classic image ID.\"\"\"\n    out = {\"config_digest\": None, \"index_digest\": None, \"index_manifests\": []}\n    with tarfile.open(path) as t:\n        names = t.getnames()\n        if \"manifest.json\" in names:\n            m = json.load(t.extractfile(\"manifest.json\"))\n            if m and m[0].get(\"Config\", \"\").startswith(\"blobs/sha256/\"):\n                out[\"config_digest\"] = \"sha256:\" + m[0][\"Config\"].split(\"/\")[-1]\n        if \"index.json\" in names:\n            raw = t.extractfile(\"index.json\").read()\n            idx = json.loads(raw)\n            out[\"index_manifests\"] = [{\"digest\": d.get(\"digest\"), \"mediaType\": d.get(\"mediaType\")} for d in idx.get(\"manifests\", [])]\n            out[\"index_digest\"] = out[\"index_manifests\"][0][\"digest\"] if len(out[\"index_manifests\"]) == 1 else None\n            out[\"index_entry_digests\"] = [d[\"digest\"] for d in out[\"index_manifests\"]]   # may include an attestation manifest next to the image manifest\n    return out\n\n\ndef archive_provenance(path):\n    \"\"\"Follow only manifests reachable from the saved archive's OCI index.\"\"\"\n    with tarfile.open(path, \"r:*\") as archive:\n        names = {member.name.removeprefix(\"./\"): member for member in archive}\n\n        def read_json(name):\n            member = names.get(name)\n            if member is None:\n                raise ValueError(\"missing OCI manifest: \" + name)\n            with archive.extractfile(member) as stream:\n                return json.load(stream)\n\n        if \"index.json\" not in names:\n            return {\"retained\": False, \"reason\": \"No OCI index.json in docker save archive\",\n                    \"attestation_manifests\": []}\n        found, seen = [], set()\n\n        def visit(desc, attestation=False):\n            digest = desc.get(\"digest\", \"\")\n            if not re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", digest) or digest in seen:\n                return\n            seen.add(digest)\n            name = \"blobs/sha256/\" + digest.split(\":\")[1]\n            doc = read_json(name)\n            marked = (attestation or desc.get(\"annotations\", {}).get(\n                \"vnd.docker.reference.type\") == \"attestation-manifest\")\n            for layer in doc.get(\"layers\", []):\n                if layer.get(\"mediaType\") != \"application/vnd.in-toto+json\":\n                    continue\n                statement = read_json(\"blobs/sha256/\" + layer[\"digest\"].split(\":\")[1])\n                if statement.get(\"predicateType\", \"\").startswith(\"https://slsa.dev/provenance/\"):\n                    # The in-toto predicate itself proves this is provenance, not just an SBOM.\n                    found.append({\"manifest\": digest, \"statement\": layer[\"digest\"],\n                                  \"predicate_type\": statement[\"predicateType\"],\n                                  \"attestation_annotation\": marked})\n            for child in doc.get(\"manifests\", []):\n                visit(child, marked)\n\n        for descriptor in read_json(\"index.json\").get(\"manifests\", []):\n            visit(descriptor)\n        return {\"retained\": bool(found), \"reason\": \"Inspected reachable OCI manifests and predicates\",\n                \"attestation_manifests\": found}\n\n\nclass Runner:\n    def __init__(self, out):\n        self.out = out\n\n    def __call__(self, command, *, cwd=None, env=None, stdout_path=None, capture=True,\n                 stderr_path=None, timeout=None):\n        # Spool process output to files: full compiler logs never accumulate in RAM.\n        with tempfile.TemporaryFile(dir=self.out) as stdout, tempfile.TemporaryFile(dir=self.out) as stderr:\n            expired = None\n            try:\n                result = subprocess.run(command, cwd=cwd, env=env, stdout=stdout, stderr=stderr,\n                                        **({\"timeout\": timeout} if timeout is not None else {}))\n            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as exc:\n                expired = exc\n            stdout.seek(0)\n            stderr.seek(0)\n            with (self.out / \"build.stdout\").open(\"ab\") as log:\n                if stdout_path:\n                    with Path(stdout_path).open(\"wb\") as target:\n                        copy_stream(stdout, target)\n                else:\n                    copy_stream(stdout, log)\n            with (self.out / \"build.stderr\").open(\"ab\") as log:\n                copy_stream(stderr, log)\n            if stderr_path:\n                stderr.seek(0)\n                with Path(stderr_path).open(\"wb\") as target:\n                    copy_stream(stderr, target)\n            if expired:\n                raise expired\n            if result.returncode:\n                raise RuntimeError(f\"Command exited {result.returncode}: {command!r}\")\n            if stdout_path or not capture:\n                return \"\"\n            stdout.seek(0)\n            return stdout.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n\n\ndef copy_stream(source, target):\n    for chunk in iter(lambda: source.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n        target.write(chunk)\n\n\ndef resolve_base(run, value, kind):\n    expected = f\"nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-{kind}-ubuntu24.04\"\n    name, separator, digest = value.partition(\"@\")\n    if name not in (expected, \"docker.io/\" + expected):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Expected {expected}, got {name}\")\n    if not separator:\n        info = json.loads(run([\"docker\", \"image\", \"inspect\", name]))[0]\n        candidates = [item.partition(\"@\")[2] for item in info.get(\"RepoDigests\", [])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('cc/build_engine/README.md')\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('Run from the campaign directory. Give every attempt a new or empty output directory. While executing assignment T-D, keep outputs under \"'`cc/build_engine/` or `builds/llamacpp/`.'\"', 'Run from the campaign directory. Give every attempt a new or empty output directory. For assignment T-N, keep outputs under \"'`cc/build_engine/` or `artifacts/codexN/`. The CLI uses the Dockerfile and Bake recipe in `cc/build_engine/recipes/`; it does not modify or use the older recipes under `builds/llamacpp/`.'\"')\ns = s.replace('\"'`build-record.json` uses schema version 1.'\"', '\"'`build-record.json` uses schema version 2. Version 1 evidence remains untouched; this capability has no build-record reader. Schema 2 adds `cmake_defines`, `recipe_sha256`, and `linkage`; `cmake_flags` includes all built-in and extra definitions.'\"')\ns = s.replace('A single short-lived \"'`docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /usr/bin/sha256sum` container hashes the tools without requesting a GPU. Subsequent hashing and saving use the immutable config ID so a later tag change cannot change the evidence target.'\"', 'A short-lived \"'`docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /bin/sh` container hashes the tools and libraries without requesting a GPU. Hashing, saving, and optional linkage inspection use the immutable `containerimage.config.digest` from Buildx metadata, because Docker image inspection can report an OCI index digest as `Id`. Missing config metadata is an explicit inspection failure.'\"')\nstart = s.index('From \"'`builds/llamacpp/`, run'\"')\nend = s.index('From the campaign directory, run:', start)\ns = s[:start] + 'The CLI stages its recipes in \"'`.campaign-recipe/` inside the archived source context. Bake receives digest-pinned base references, source and patch identity, extra targets, and extra definitions from the CLI. Prefer the CLI for validation and evidence collection; direct builds using the older `builds/llamacpp/` recipes do not support these variant options.'\"\\\\n\\\\n' + s[end:]\ns = s.replace('No full build was performed for T-D.', 'No Docker execution or network access was performed for T-N.')\ninsert = '''## Engine variants and linkage\n\nUse repeatable \"'`--cmake-define KEY=VALUE` options. Keys must match `''^[A-Z0-9_]+$`; values must be nonempty and contain only ASCII letters, digits, or `_./:+,@%=-`. Whitespace, shell metacharacters, empty values, duplicate keys (even with identical values), and all built-in keys are rejected before output creation. This also reserves the built-in compiler-launcher and executable-linker flags. Definitions are sorted by key, passed as the `CMAKE_DEFINES` build argument as space-separated `-DKEY=VALUE` words, and stored in the runtime image label `campaign.cmake.defines` in that same format. The CLI overwrites inherited `CMAKE_DEFINES` environment values.\n\n`recipes` records the SHA256 and size of each recipe file. `recipe_sha256` hashes canonical JSON (sorted keys, compact separators) containing those file identities, all built-in flags, the definitions, and extra targets. Definition values therefore change recipe identity even when recipe bytes are unchanged; reordering definitions does not.\n\nFor the GPU budget shim, build with VMM disabled at compile time. From the campaign root, with a clean source checkout at the shown commit and local base images available:\n\n```bash\npython3 cc/build_engine/build_engine.py '\"\\\\\\\\\n  --source ref/llama.cpp --commit 31288c9c66e59377f7788d920678a565bb89dd37 \\\\\\\\\n  --tag campaign/llamacpp:no-vmm \\\\\\\\\n  --out artifacts/codexN/no-vmm-build \\\\\\\\\n  --cmake-define GGML_CUDA_NO_VMM=ON \\\\\\\\\n  --linkage\n\"'```\n\n`--linkage` enables a final check after saving the image and collecting provenance. It runs one additional `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /bin/sh` against the built image'\"'s config ID, with a 60-second client timeout and no GPU. It discovers \"'`/app/libggml-cuda.so` or a versioned `/app/libggml-cuda.so.*`, runs `ldd`, and selects `readelf -Ws` or, if unavailable, `nm -D`. A pass requires a dynamic `libcudart.so*` dependency and undefined imports of exactly `cudaMalloc`, `cudaFree`, and `cudaMemGetInfo` (including versioned symbols). Other CUDA API names and defined symbols do not satisfy the check. `ldd` showing `libcudart.so.12 => not found` still establishes a dynamic dependency; this check does not establish that runtime dependencies resolve on the GPU host.\n\nThe record'\"'s \"'`linkage` object contains `status` (`not_requested`, `passed`, `failed`, or `unavailable`), the discovered library, config ID, `libcudart_dynamic`, `undefined_imports`, each tool'\"'s return code/reason, and output paths. Missing tools, a missing library, nonzero tool exits, Docker failures, timeouts, and malformed probe output are \"'`unavailable`; unavailable measurements are JSON null rather than false. Runtime images may lack both readelf and nm: the check explicitly records this rather than installing tools or silently claiming imports are absent.\n\nA failed or unavailable requested check sets top-level `failure_stage=\"linkage\"` and exits 1, while preserving the saved archive and other evidence. `--linkage-optional` enables the same check (even without `--linkage`) but permits a failed/unavailable result with overall success and exit 0; inspect `linkage.status` in that case. With neither flag, linkage is `not_requested`.\n\nThe probe saves `linkage.raw.txt` (framed stdout), `linkage.stderr.txt` (Docker/probe stderr), `linkage.ldd.txt`, and `linkage.symbols.txt`. Tool stderr is merged into its corresponding raw tool output. On a Docker error or malformed probe, only the first two files may be available. This ELF check does not prove allocation interception, actual pool selection, or GPU execution; the orchestrator must verify `NO_VMM = 1` and allocation events under the budget shim.\n\n'\"'''\ns = s.replace('## Outputs and failure handling\\\\n', insert + '## Outputs and failure handling\\\\n')\ns = s.replace('They use no network, GPU, or real build.', 'They also cover define validation, variant recipe identity/build arguments/labels, schema 2, captured ELF linkage fixtures, shell tool selection, config-ID versus index-ID targeting, and fatal/optional linkage failures. They use no network, GPU, or real engine build.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > cc/build_engine/fixtures/README.md <<'EOF'\nThese are captured host \"'`ldd`, `readelf -Ws`, and `nm -D` outputs for a CPU-only\nELF fixture, not a CUDA engine. A mock `libcudart.so.12` defines three dummy\nfunctions; a shared `libggml-cuda.so` calls them and leaves them as imports.\nThe sources and compiled fixture are under `artifacts/codexN/linkage-fixture/`.\nThe fixture has an `$ORIGIN` runpath. Addresses and absolute paths are incidental;\ntests parse library and symbol names only. No Docker, CUDA toolkit, or GPU was used.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
