not prove allocation interception, actual pool selection, or GPU execution; the orchestrator must verify `NO_VMM = 1` and allocation events under the budget shim.\n\n'\"'''\ns = s.replace('## Outputs and failure handling\\\\n', insert + '## Outputs and failure handling\\\\n')\ns = s.replace('They use no network, GPU, or real build.', 'They also cover define validation, variant recipe identity/build arguments/labels, schema 2, captured ELF linkage fixtures, shell tool selection, config-ID versus index-ID targeting, and fatal/optional linkage failures. They use no network, GPU, or real engine build.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > cc/build_engine/fixtures/README.md <<'EOF'\nThese are captured host \"'`ldd`, `readelf -Ws`, and `nm -D` outputs for a CPU-only\nELF fixture, not a CUDA engine. A mock `libcudart.so.12` defines three dummy\nfunctions; a shared `libggml-cuda.so` calls them and leaves them as imports.\nThe sources and compiled fixture are under `artifacts/codexN/linkage-fixture/`.\nThe fixture has an `$ORIGIN` runpath. Addresses and absolute paths are incidental;\ntests parse library and symbol names only. No Docker, CUDA toolkit, or GPU was used.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
